<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cathedral of Saint Demetrius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1194–1197</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cathedral of Saint Demetrius is a white-stone church in Vladimir, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, built in 1194–1197 by Grand Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vsevolod-the-big-nest">Vsevolod the Big Nest</a> as his palace church. It is famous for the hundreds of carved reliefs of saints, animals, birds and mythical beasts that cover its upper walls. It is part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-monuments-of-vladimir-and-suzdal">White Monuments of Vladimir and Suzdal</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cathedral-of-saint-demetrius.jpg" alt="Cathedral of Saint Demetrius" width="320" height="368" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ludvig14 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vladimir_StDemetriusCathedral_6875.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
